.Dd March 2, 2026
.Dt ELF_OPEN_MEMORY_NOCOPY 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm elf_open_memory_nocopy
.Nd open an ELF object from memory without copying the backing buffer
.Sh LIBRARY
libelfobj
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In elfobj.h
.Ft elf_err_t
.Fn elf_open_memory_nocopy "const void *buf" "size_t size" "elfobj_t **out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn elf_open_memory_nocopy
parses ELF data directly from
.Fa buf
without taking ownership or copying input bytes.
The caller must keep the buffer valid until
.Fn elf_close
is called on the resulting object.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns
.Dv ELF_OK
on success, otherwise an
.Vt elf_err_t
code.
.Sh ERRORS
Possible errors include
.Dv ELF_ERR_STATE ,
.Dv ELF_ERR_OOM ,
and ELF parse/format errors.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr elf_close 3 ,
.Xr elf_open_memory 3
